module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.an_edge_index_spells_each_endpoint_once_per_occurrence

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// A COST MODE MEASURED ON THE HEAL ROUND, NOT INFERRED FROM A COMMENT. The surface is a corpus that
// looks like it outgrew a ceiling; the question this mode answers is what a container costs PER ITEM
// IT NAMES (gunbc.design_argument::how_to_work: "a proven cost-shape defect -- a copied accumulator,
// a quadratic fold -- is *always fixed*, regardless of realized n").
data an_edge_index_spells_each_endpoint_once_per_occurrence: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "an_edge_index_spells_each_endpoint_once_per_occurrence" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the heal round's regen scope round refuses at the CI ceiling on a 176-file extdeps frontier drain -- run 43753613457, job 132966002648, head 1672899b219b: MemoryStallRefusedPageThrash, slot 26.85 GB, no answer line -- while the same round answers in about 9 s at 16.05 GB when its scope is empty (runs 43702995862, 43702268835). A phase-level trace cannot act on that, so the round was measured structure by structure (measurement-only head 6d0572746e5c, run 43754559395): the scope child enters at 3 MB and already holds 6.97 GB before it reads the change; its closure edge index then grows the resident set by 5.56 GB while holding rows=8,696 whose 2,057,713 endpoint occurrences spell 71,694,634 bytes.",

    "THE SHAPE, IN ONE NUMBER: 71.7 MB of path bytes held by 5.56 GB of resident set -- the container costs 77x the data it names. Two redundancies carry it. A row is the union of the FULL import closure of every provider the file references, and that closure was walked, spelled and owned once per REQUESTING file rather than once per provider. And every endpoint occurrence was a separate owned `String`, which the interpreter's `Value::Str` then spelled AGAIN on the way to the model. The 6.97 GB before the change is read: the scope child resolves the whole corpus to answer its own worktree admission, and the edge-index route built its own second whole-corpus index with build_multi_entry_index beside the process-shared one the same child had already built, so one process parsed and typechecked the corpus twice.",

    "THE REPAIR, REPRESENTATION ONLY: one interned `Rc<str>` per workspace-relative module path for the process, so rows, the edge list and the model's edge arguments share the same bytes; a provider's import closure expanded once per facts build and shared, the expansion being a pure function of (facts build, provider path) -- the same key the facts memo already uses; and the edge list deduplicated by MODULE RANK, ranks taken from the sorted module roster, which reproduces the emitted (from, to) pairs pair-for-pair and in the same order the set form produced. The edge SET, the closure and the arm are untouched: which modules regen is decided by the same relation as before, and the scoped round's host-versus-model lockstep refuses the line on disagreement every run. The witness is the Rust test that compares the emitted pairs with the spelled ones and asserts one allocation per module name across the whole list.",

    "PART OF THE RUNG STAYS UNREAD: before the repair the mode is MEASURED at the runs named above; after it the shape is unread -- no run has carried a 176-file frontier drain through a repaired scope round -- so the row does not borrow a number from the shape argument. The rung is readable when such a run names its resident set and its member count.",

    "THE RELATION QUESTION, ANSWERED AS MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN ARGUMENT: the host repair above left the round dying in the model evaluating 2,065,084 closure-expanded rows (run 43808654519: the model phase at 12.81 GB holding those rows, then MemoryStallRefusedPageThrash after 2,131,492 ms with no progress). The question was whether the expansion carries answer. A probe over the round's OWN pool built the candidate relations and walked each with the route's own reverse-walk function over nine edited sets (measurement-only head 00a0fcd0419f, run 43817027204): the route's generator -- its parsed reference targets plus the bare-name provider edges for exactly the files the bare half runs for -- spells 61,044 rows against the 2,065,084, and its affected member sets are identical on every set (admit2-equal=9, admit2-lost=0, admit2-gained=0). The expansion bought rows and no reach, so the regen scope round is handed the generator and the model's walk takes the closure. What stays UNMEASURED after the change is the emission phase over an affected set of 5,857 members, which no drain-shaped round has reached: the rung remains unread until a run names its resident set, its member count and its wall.",

    "ONE CONSUMER'S REUSE, SCOPED HONESTLY: the one-index-per-process reuse this row's repair introduced lands only when the demanding route's pool is the pool the process already resolved. On the heal route they differ -- the regen scope round's pool is `src/v1` plus `dag` while the process pool the same child resolved for the model is `dag` plus `src/v2` -- and the shared build is refused with `SharedIndexSecondResidentPool` (run 43784443590), so that route still pays the cold build and prints the located cause line. Naming the case keeps the degradation countable instead of reading as closed (gunbc.design_argument::fail_closed).
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.regen_affected_set", decl_name: "regen_affected_set", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.regen_affected_set", decl_name: "regen_reverse_closure", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.self_host_regen_affected_set_witness", decl_name: "a_reverse_closure_reaches_transitive_dependents_only", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
